how's it going everybody so I've got a  lot of personal DMS with questions about  the James gun incident that happened the  past few days I wasn't going to do a  video on this because I didn't want my  personal opinion out there on the matter  but a lot of you have been asking me  what exactly happened why he got fired  because all you heard is that he got  fired and what it means for the future  of the guardians of the galaxy 3 and the  MCU so in this video I'll simply explain  the events that took place over the past  weekend why James gun was fired and what  it could possibly mean for the future of  the guardians of the galaxy and MCU in a  nutshell James gun was fired for some  tweets that he made back in 2010 that  concern rape and pedophilia recently  they've been brought back to the surface  and Disney has made the executive  decision to fire him from guardians of  the galaxy 3 here's what Disney had to  say about the situation the offensive  attitudes and statements discovered on  James's Twitter feed are indefensible  and inconsistent with our Studios values  and we have severed our business  relationship with him the interesting  thing is that James already had  apologized for these tweets back in 2012  when Disney had hired him to direct the  first guardians of the galaxy movie so  was Disney ok with this back in 2012 and  now that it's been brought back into the  light again and people are making a big  deal about it they're not okay with it  that's a question that will most likely  never have an answer to but of course  James Gunn has come out and apologized  for these tweets again he also issued a  final statement regarding the matter  when he closed his Twitter account with  his final tweet saying many people who  have followed my career know when I  started I viewed myself as a provocateur  making movies and telling jokes that  were outrageous and taboo as I have  discussed publicly many times as I've  developed as a person so has my work and  my humor he also issued this official  apology to the public my words of nearly  a decade ago were at the time totally  failed and unfortunate efforts to be  provocative I have regretted them for  many years since not just because they  were stupid not at all funny wildly  insensitive and certainly not  provocative like I had hoped but also  because they don't reflect the person I  am today or have been for some time  regardless of how much time has passed  I understand and accept the business  decision taken today even these many  years later I take full responsibility  for the way I conducted myself then all  I can do now be on offering my sincere  and heartfelt regret is to be the best  human being I can be accepting  understanding committed to equality and  far more thoughtful about my public  statements and my obligations to our  public discourse to everyone inside of  my industry and beyond I again offer my  deepest apologies love to all so what  does this mean for James Gunn and  guardians of the galaxy 3 well there's  already a petition going around for  James Gunn to be rehired to direct a  movie the petition already has over  200,000 signatures with the goal of  getting 300,000 but will this even be  enough James Gunn was going to play a  huge role in the cosmic expansion of the  MCU exploring characters like Adam  warlock the Eternals and characters that  we have not seen yet so James Gunn is  certainly very very valuable to Disney  and the MCU but it does not seem like  Disney's going to be very forgiving on  this the Guardians cast is certainly all  shook up and very heartbroken some  members have stepped up and started to  defend James Gunn saying that he's a  very genuine and great guy while some  have taken to Twitter to express their  heartbreak Zoe Saldana said it's been a  challenging weekend I'm not gonna lie  I'm pausing myself to take everything in  before I speak out of turn I just want  everyone to know I love all members of  my guardians of the galaxy family always  will Chris Pratt took to Twitter quoting  a Bible verse understand this my  brothers and sisters let every person be  quick to listen slow to speak slow to  anger James 1:19 and Karen Gillan also  spoke up saying love to every single  member of my guardians of the galaxy  family just to clarify I'll speak more  on this later but just wanted to make  sure that was out there love to you all  so the cast and the fans are all  certainly very devastated and  heartbroken but will this be enough for  Disney to change their minds and if they  don't change their minds and James Gunn  is out for good what will happen to  guardians of the galaxy 3 and the MCU I  think there are two different routes  that they could take to keep the MCU as  great as it is now and to keep moving  forward in the right direction I think  one of the routes that they could take  is Josh Whedon who is a part of big  things like agents of shield the first  Avengers movie in Avengers age of Ultron  and then of course the Russo brothers  who directed Avengers infinity war and  Avengers 4 we would obviously all love  for James Gunn to return but if he  doesn't I would feel the most  comfortable if the future of the MCU was  in the hands of the reso brothers and  Josh Whedon who do you all think would  be best to take over guardians of the  galaxy and help with the expansion of  the MCU let me know your thoughts in the  comments below hit the like button and  don't forget to subscribe to my channel  so you can stay up to date on all things  Marvel DC and superhero thank you all so  much for watching woof woof  [Music]  you  [Music]
 

